WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.460
kanashimi sasou midnight

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.460
Such a sad midnight,

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:09.400
koboreru ai o choudai

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:09.400
overflowing with love.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.970
kiiroi ringo o kajitteru

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.910
Gnawing at a yellow apple,

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.930
kimi wa hitoshirezu otona ni naru

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.930
you secretly become an adult.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.370
tameiki iro shite mayoikomu

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.370
You sigh, having lost your way

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.140
ai o sagashite ikiteru

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.140
living in a search for love.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.420
suki yo tabun ne dakedo

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.420
Maybe I love you, but—

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.860
akai tsuki ga miteru

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.860
the red moon is watching,

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:45.450
konna ni mo chikaku ni iru no ni

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:45.450
it waits nearby.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.910
kanashimi sasou midnight

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.910
Such a sad midnight.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.980
I can say love

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.710
koboreru ai o choudai

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.710
It overflows with love.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:53.710
will you love me?

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:57.320
tomadoi no hitomi no oku

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:57.320
Lost within your eyes,

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.270
kokyuu o tomete

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.270
I stop breathing.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.830
kimi no ai o katachi ni

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.830
The shape of your love,

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.480
mayonaka no taiyou

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.480
is like the midnight sun.

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:25.250
Driving the Da Ruma guild into extinction in such a short time

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.550
was impressive indeed!

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:27.850
Excellent work, Airi-sama!

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:29.390
Thanks!

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:33.820
It must be lonely for your cherished member now that his job is obsolete.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:42.630
After everything that's gone on, I still have training to do, don't I...

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.540
That doesn't go there!

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:55.680
So you came all this way here just to say that?

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.310
No, of course not.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:02.440
We would like the Galaxy Army to put the Kamidake to use from now on.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:10.150
Pursuit

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.920
You're lucky this is all you suffered.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.690
I would've expected much more serious injuries than this!

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:16.920
It's because I'm used to getting hurt...

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.120
There, all done.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:22.160
Maybe I shouldn't be so surprised,

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:24.260
you did destroy the Da Ruma guild, after all!

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:24.900
Huh?!

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.090
I think you're the greatest...

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:30.730
I'm all better now! Thank you!

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:37.140
Well, I need to hurry to my next duty station.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:40.680
Transfer it to the military? I don't like the sound of that...

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:43.110
Might you be trying to start a war somewhere?

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.420
Nothing of the sort.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:48.950
It's just that restricting it to the GP's decoy unit is a waste of a great asset.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:52.020
I see. That is a sound argument...

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:55.890
Well, I've only come here to greet you today, so I shall take my leave now.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:59.160
Documents from the Galactic Union should arrive very soon,

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.700
so I ask for your cooperation when that time comes.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.390
Understood.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:08.910
Airi-sama.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:11.310
Quicker than we expected, wasn't it?

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:14.340
"Safety First"

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:17.480
T-This is a pet...?

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:21.520
The current fad. It says in the book how to take care of 'em.

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:22.250
I see...

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:25.620
I have to go attend to the other animals now, so she's all yours.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.090
Right!

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:29.630
Let's see, what should I do...?

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:31.690
Food, I bet?

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:36.990
Let's see... Food...

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.800
Why?!

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.440
Why do we have to give the Kamidake to the army?!

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:44.710
--There's no need to shout! --But...!

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:46.610
It's an official document.

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:49.110
There's no room for protest when you're given one of these.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:50.350
So then...

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:52.450
But the Kamidake is linked with Mizuki!

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:54.950
Only the Kamidake is to switch hands.

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:58.560
There's no way we could hand over an individual's royal ship.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.160
But the Kamidake belongs to Seina!

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:04.230
Washu-sama gave it to him...

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:06.900
Unfortunately, that isn't the case.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:11.370
Documents pertaining to ship disposal on Planet Jurai are incomplete.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:14.910
So the current Kamidake is considered a remodel of the first Kamidake.

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:17.640
Basically, that means it's still a GP ship.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:20.380
Then why don't we contact Washu-sama right away

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:22.250
and have its name changed?

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:24.620
That would only be a temporary solution -

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:27.190
- the army would find a way to take it sooner or later.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:30.660
In that case, there's no need to unlink Mizuki from it, Kiriko!

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.090
If we insist that Mizuki belongs to Kiriko,

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:34.490
we can make their registration process come to a grinding halt!

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:36.490
What a childish idea.

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:39.160
Do you really think they would care?

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:42.030
They would be more than happy to get a royal ship as an added bonus,

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:43.700
and it would only cause a big stir if they did...

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:46.500
Or perhaps you feel like being arrested for interfering with official affairs?

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:51.510
Even if it is an ordinary transfer or if it's for technological examination,

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:56.250
the Galaxy Army is a branch of the GP, so there's no room for argument.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:05:00.990
It's only natural for them to want Professor Washu's masterpiece -

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:04.360
- it and its key mechanism are as powerful as a royal ship.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:07.630
Does "them" refer to Jurai...?

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:08.650
Of course.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:13.870
After all, the technology is so advanced that it threatens Jurai's superiority.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:17.840
The same goes for the Academy, which is threatened by unemployment.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:22.210
But that doesn't mean Jurai can just go and analyze it whenever it wants.

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:26.310
All that would do is put other nearby nations on unnecessary alert.

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:28.110
Something like that, anyway.

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.780
So you're going to use Fuku-chan as a political tool?!

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:34.320
That's right. That's the type of position I'm in.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:35.190
Airi-sama!

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:39.420
Didn't you say before that Fuku-chan is Washu-sama's daughter...?!

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:40.660
It's useless!

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:43.460
These are orders, aren't they, Airi-dono?

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:44.760
That's right.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.830
How can they seriously do this?!

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:51.500
I won't let them have her! I won't let them have Fuku-chan!

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:52.800
Hey, wait! I'm coming too!

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:54.930
Oh! Kiriko-san! Amane-san!

00:05:57.780 --> 00:05:59.480
Seto-sama.

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:03.480
I realize I may be a political tool myself.

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:08.020
But now I want to act of my own accord, as Neige.

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:10.450
Look after Kiriko-chan and the others, okay?

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:28.240
I won't let them have her!

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.170
Let me talk to Seina Yamada!

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:34.980
Oh, him! Missed his duel the other day, did you?

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:36.950
Just hurry up!

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:42.990
Why does it take this long to register a ship?!

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:45.720
It looks like there's a lot of network traffic

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:47.430
because the administrative computers are undergoing maintenance.

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:49.530
The administrative computers? Why?

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:51.460
I bet Airi-sama or Seto-sama is behind this...

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:53.030
Most likely.

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:54.200
So what should we do?

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:57.670
Create a bypass and have the Kamidake process the information.

00:06:57.670 --> 00:07:01.140
The best computer in the Academy is sitting right here.

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:05.780
What we're talking about is illegal hacking and could get us in big trouble.

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:07.410
Are you sure about this?

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:09.650
I won't force you to if you don't want to.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:10.980
Have you forgotten?

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:14.410
I'm a pirate!

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:17.820
You seem to be enjoying yourself.

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:22.290
Now the other side will have to speed things up, too...

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:27.200
It looks like Kiriko-chan has completely forgotten

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:29.570
that she's an intelligence officer under your direct control.

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:31.900
But what's wrong with that?

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:39.500
It takes time to become an iron-willed old hag like Seto-sama here.

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:44.370
Well then, what do you say we begin our cleanup?

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:51.790
Looks like you're done.

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:53.760
Yes, we are. How about you, Amane?

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:55.330
Did you get in touch with Seina-chan?

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:57.860
No, apparently there was an accident during his training,

00:07:57.860 --> 00:07:59.430
so he didn't have time to see me.

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:02.130
What could he be doing at a time like this?

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:04.500
H-Help!

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:05.670
What're you doing?

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:07.270
What does it look like? I'm trying to give her food...

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:09.640
No, it looks like you're the food...

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:12.140
So were you able to change the ship's registration?

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:15.150
If the army doesn't do anything for 3 - no, 2 days - then we'll have won!

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:18.680
Our transfer orders go into effect in 4 days, so this should be a cinch!

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:21.050
Huh? Where are Neige-sama and Fuku-chan?

00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:23.620
They went back to Amane-san's penthouse.

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:25.960
She said it was Fuku-chan's lunchtime or something...

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:28.290
Oh. She sure has it easy, doesn't she?

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:32.760
What are you doing here?!

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:35.900
It appears your removal of the Mizuki unit is complete.

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:38.100
These are orders from the executive office of the Galaxy Army.

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:42.110
The Galaxy Army is now in control of the Kamidake.

00:08:42.110 --> 00:08:42.940
What?!

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:46.340
You're too early! You're not supposed to be taking it for a few more days!

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:48.110
Seina Yamada and the rest of his crew

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:51.220
are hereby relieved of their duties aboard the Kamidake.

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:55.580
You are to return to headquarters immediately for further orders.

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:05.630
What could all the old ladies be doing?

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:08.390
Everything's OK now, though...

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:15.200
H-Hey! Fuku-chan!

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:20.340
Fuku-chan...?!

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:32.190
Neige Na Melmas-sama.

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:37.330
We are confiscating the Kamidake's AI unit as it is now military property.

00:09:37.330 --> 00:09:38.760
This is no different than a robbery.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:42.230
And you're even rude enough to hide your faces from your victim...

00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:45.970
That is because we can't be sure you won't use your abilities.

00:09:45.970 --> 00:09:49.540
Please forgive our weak and cowardly actions.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:51.780
I'm home...

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:54.010
Today was definitely not a good day...

00:09:57.350 --> 00:09:58.710
Forgive me...

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:03.620
Is somebody here?!

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:11.800
Neige-chan! What's wrong? What happened?!

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:13.500
I'm so sorry, Big Brother...

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:14.330
Fuku-chan's gone...

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:15.420
She's gone...?!

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:41.760
This is Seina Yamada, captain of the Kamidake!

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:46.100
I request that you return Fuku and the Kamidake immediately!

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:49.300
So you're the famous Lorelei Seina-dono?

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:51.240
It's an honor to meet you.

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:54.340
It's useless. I don't feel a thing.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:56.310
I'm sorry, though.

00:10:56.310 --> 00:10:58.910
The decision to do this was made by the Galactic Union.

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:02.650
We are simply carrying out our orders.

00:11:02.650 --> 00:11:04.420
I have no choice in the matter...

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:06.350
Hyperspace jump preparations complete!

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:07.990
We're in a hurry. Goodbye.

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:09.450
Wait, I still have more to
--

00:11:09.450 --> 00:11:12.120
Darn it! Now what?!

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:15.190
Even if I could follow them, I have no idea where they went...

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:18.330
You're so lucky... You're still energetic...

00:11:18.330 --> 00:11:20.700
Come to think of it, you haven't been in very high spirits lately, NB...

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:23.970
It's hopeless. Ever since that night, I've been...

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:25.640
You're gonna chase that ship, right?

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:26.670
But I dunno where it went...

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:31.810
Don't worry, I accessed the ship's dressing room just a minute ago.

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:33.610
For real?!

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:36.680
But this ship doesn't have a Deep Space Unit...

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:39.450
Women are full of secrets.

00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:40.720
Women are scary!

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:41.380
Huh?

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:03.070
We jumped...?

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:06.080
I didn't know it had a Deep Space Unit...!

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:08.010
But more importantly...

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:12.980
You are approaching private space. Please alter your course.

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:14.550
What does this mean?

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:17.320
If I change my course now I'll lose Fuku...

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:18.310
My only choice is to keep going!

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:25.130
What?! Seina went after the Kamidake?!

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:26.660
In Kiriko's cruiser...

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:27.500
Oh no...

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:28.870
Talk about reckless...

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:31.440
Worst case scenario, he'll wind up in a fight with the army...

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:36.030
That's a good possibility, judging from Big Brother Seina's bad luck...

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:38.840
That's fine if he is fighting with them...

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:39.780
Chairwoman!

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:42.650
What a frightening expression. It's unbecoming of your beauty.

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:45.620
Um, what did you mean about fighting against the military?

00:12:45.620 --> 00:12:49.650
The military transport ship and the Kamidake have gone missing.

00:12:49.650 --> 00:12:51.660
Apparently they didn't show up at their scheduled rendezvous point

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:54.290
where military representatives were waiting for them.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:57.190
Neither did Seina's cruiser, of course.

00:12:57.190 --> 00:12:59.830
You don't mean he's already gotten into a fight with them?!

00:12:59.830 --> 00:13:00.930
It's anyone's guess.

00:13:00.930 --> 00:13:04.330
Either way, the fact that this has turned into a big mess hasn't changed.

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:09.610
Misao-chan!

00:13:09.610 --> 00:13:14.710
Kiriko Masaki. Amane Kaunaq. Ryoko Balouta. Neige Na Melmas.

00:13:14.710 --> 00:13:16.010
You are hereby under arrest

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:19.520
for suspicion of aiding in the destruction and hijacking of transport ships.

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.320
What's going on, Misao-chan?!

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:24.320
Amane-san. Please stop calling me "chan"!

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:28.190
What do you mean we aided in the destruction and hijacking of ships?

00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:29.230
Misao-chan!

00:13:29.230 --> 00:13:31.690
Not you too, Kiriko-san...

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:37.570
GP Academy student trainee pursued the Kamidake,

00:13:37.570 --> 00:13:40.340
and shortly afterward we lost all contact with the transport ship.

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:42.410
He's suspected of destroying the transport ship

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:44.880
and commandeering the Kamidake.

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:48.780
What?! Seina-sama would never do any such thing!

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:50.650
We're about to look into that.

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:55.320
Come on, I even sang songs for you at your wedding with Mashisu!

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:59.520
I appreciate it, but please refrain from doing that again.

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:03.060
Anyway, come with me.

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:06.500
We wouldn't want to put your family standings in jeopardy.

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:16.070
How far are they gonna keep going?

00:14:16.070 --> 00:14:18.700
Get involved with women and you'll get burned.

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:22.870
Looks like Saturn.

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:28.440
A blue planet... An Earth-class planet?

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:32.890
What was that?!

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:35.380
ID signal red! Pirates...?!

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:39.700
Might not be so bad to kick the bucket out here...

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:41.030
Remnants of the Da Ruma guild? No, they're not!

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:43.800
Where's our weapons?!

00:14:44.470 --> 00:14:46.160
We don't have any at all?!

00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:53.680
Please make yourselves at home.

00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:55.480
So this is the Kuramitsu family's second residence...

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:57.610
This is a pretty nice reception you're giving us.

00:14:57.610 --> 00:14:59.880
Any other way and you would complain.

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:02.950
You will be living here during the investigation.

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:04.620
So it's a fancy form of house arrest?

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:07.460
Please forgive me. I'm a military man.

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:11.900
But you're free to use anything here for the duration of your stay.

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:13.060
Anything at all.

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:15.260
Now if you'll excuse me.

00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:19.340
Kiriko!

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:21.460
Yes. This, right?

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:27.280
What is this...?!

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:29.510
The very latest supercomputer workstation!

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:31.650
He wants us to use this to figure out what's going on!

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:34.080
Maybe I'll sing a song for him later...

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:45.460
I'm glad I was able to make an emergency landing,

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:48.120
but the pirates can't be very far away either...!

00:15:49.870 --> 00:15:54.200
You seen a Deep Space Cruiser around here?

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:56.410
N-No...! I haven't seen anything!

00:15:56.410 --> 00:15:57.510
Alright, then.

00:15:57.510 --> 00:15:59.380
You a water thief?

00:15:59.380 --> 00:16:01.900
I'll use you as a warning to the rest of your village.

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:06.820
Stop it!

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:15.680
Look out!

00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:24.290
Are you all right?

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:33.080
Thank you so much for saving my son!

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:35.610
It was nothing, I am in the GP...

00:16:35.610 --> 00:16:38.220
And besides... It might have been my fault...

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:39.020
Come again?

00:16:39.020 --> 00:16:40.080
No, nothing...

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:43.750
Oh! You're the legendary hero!

00:16:45.760 --> 00:16:49.030
To think that I would be able to meet the Hero in my lifetime...!

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:50.990
Now our village has nothing to fear!

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:52.300
Eh? Huh?

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:54.200
You probably shouldn't take him too seriously.

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:58.140
He says the same thing to every stranger who comes into our village!

00:16:58.140 --> 00:16:59.700
I almost thought I was in an RPG...

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:03.160
Villagers! Tonight we'll have a welcoming celebration for our new visitor!

00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:06.710
Eh? Um, I have things to take attend to...

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:08.250
Oh, come on!

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:09.710
Yeah!

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:11.410
O-Okay...

00:17:14.990 --> 00:17:17.050
I found the cruiser!

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:18.960
Get any information from it?

00:17:18.960 --> 00:17:21.430
Nope. Couldn't with the firewall he set up.

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:23.290
But I did find this thing!

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:27.130
No good. I'm not feeling a thing. Not even with Kiriko-san's panties...

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:33.370
Um, I'm glad you're welcoming me here,

00:17:33.370 --> 00:17:34.440
but who are these people?

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:37.510
They're attendants who come with this seat of honor, of course!

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:39.580
As the saying goes, "Great men prefer great women."

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:41.010
I don't think that's quite it...

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:43.310
Perhaps this isn't enough women to please the Hero...?

00:17:43.310 --> 00:17:44.920
No, that's not it!

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:47.020
Drink some more, Mr. Hero!

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:48.990
Uh, I'm underage...

00:17:48.990 --> 00:17:51.860
I'm so honored to meet the Hero!

00:17:51.860 --> 00:17:54.420
I'm trying to tell you, I'm not your Hero...

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:55.630
I'm so happy!

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:58.230
Now we don't have to be afraid of them anymore!

00:17:58.230 --> 00:18:01.030
But what are pirates doing in a place like this?

00:18:01.030 --> 00:18:02.130
I don't know.

00:18:02.130 --> 00:18:06.900
After this planet's owner died, they suddenly showed up and built a base.

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:09.470
They ruined our fields, destroyed our homes,

00:18:09.470 --> 00:18:11.280
and sucked up most of the underground water,

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:13.040
which dried up the wells in our village.

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:16.380
So I decided to go to their base to steal some water...

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:17.510
And then today...

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:22.720
You know, if you contact the GP, they can get rid of the pirates for you!

00:18:22.720 --> 00:18:23.620
Really?!

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:27.420
Yeah! So could you give me the details about them?

00:18:27.420 --> 00:18:28.990
Details...

00:18:28.990 --> 00:18:34.400
Come to think of it, they called themselves the Shank Guild.

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:36.230
The Shank Guild?

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:38.100
Don't tell me you mean Tarant Shank!

00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:42.090
You know him?! That's the name of their boss!

00:18:49.780 --> 00:18:52.550
We've severed her link with the Kamidake.

00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:55.920
Brain waves are at a low frequency but steady.

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:03.690
Tarant...

00:19:03.690 --> 00:19:07.660
What is he doing here? Research?

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:09.200
Is something wrong?

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:11.540
The military took off with the Kamidake.

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:15.140
I followed them into private space...

00:19:15.140 --> 00:19:17.270
Then I was attacked by pirates...

00:19:17.270 --> 00:19:20.010
And Tarant had a base on a nearby planet...

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:21.140
It couldn't be!

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:23.180
The military and Tarant are connected?!

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:24.150
Hey...

00:19:24.150 --> 00:19:25.650
Fuku's in danger!

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:28.050
Why won't you dissect it?

00:19:28.050 --> 00:19:31.560
She's a piece of incredible technology.

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:37.430
Inside this delicate creature is enough energy to fill a small universe.

00:19:37.430 --> 00:19:42.470
I don't think there's anyone who could disassemble something like this.

00:19:42.470 --> 00:19:47.070
Plus she's also been equipped with a powerful defensive mechanism.

00:19:47.070 --> 00:19:48.870
What about cloning?

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:50.270
Well...

00:19:51.640 --> 00:19:56.310
We've tried creating a number of them from hair and saliva samples,

00:19:56.310 --> 00:19:58.680
but although they appear the same as the original,

00:19:58.680 --> 00:20:00.720
they're nothing but ordinary animals.

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:02.780
Useless.

00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:12.120
Ryo-Ohki Types. Such annoying ships.

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:15.060
Tarant-sama!

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:20.230
Seina Yamada has been located! Sector D32!

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:24.070
That's crazy! You can't go alone!

00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:25.810
You'll die if you go to their base!

00:20:25.810 --> 00:20:27.440
But I have to rescue Fuku!

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:29.280
He truly is the Hero!

00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:31.250
Grandfather, stop with that already!

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:34.620
What the...?!

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:35.780
It's them!

00:20:40.890 --> 00:20:44.960
Tarant-sama's orders! Capture Seina Yamada alive!

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:46.900
But the villagers are fair game, right?

00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:48.520
Don't get too carried away now!

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:59.140
Everyone flee into the temple!

00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:06.220
Damn them...!

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:07.620
We have to hurry!

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:08.190
But...!

00:21:08.190 --> 00:21:09.850
Come on!

00:21:19.600 --> 00:21:21.900
Have you found Lorelei Seina?!

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:24.800
He seems to have fled with the villagers into the mountains.

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:40.050
It appears everyone has escaped unharmed.

00:21:40.050 --> 00:21:42.350
There's nothing to worry about in here!

00:21:42.350 --> 00:21:45.460
They don't know about this temple!

00:21:45.460 --> 00:21:46.690
But it doesn't seem like a temple...

00:21:46.690 --> 00:21:51.130
This is a holy ground where we worship our god.

00:21:51.130 --> 00:21:52.530
Look up there.

00:21:58.170 --> 00:22:01.810
That is our god.

00:22:01.810 --> 00:22:04.540
W-What is this?!

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:27.020
You're the worst, most hopeless, most unlucky boy in all of space...

00:22:32.260 --> 00:22:34.890
Even against your will... (You fail.)

00:22:34.890 --> 00:22:36.700
Even when you're gentle... (You're extremely clumsy.)

00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:41.200
With too much fighting spirit, in vain, it's all coming to nothing...

00:22:41.200 --> 00:22:44.190
You're gonna fail.

00:22:45.370 --> 00:22:48.040
Carefully... (So irritating!)

00:22:48.040 --> 00:22:50.040
Or with violence... (Ow! Quit it!)

00:22:50.040 --> 00:23:01.110
You're the worst and most hopeless... you're a lost cause.

00:23:05.560 --> 00:23:10.830
You're the worst and the most hopeless...

00:23:10.830 --> 00:23:15.170
You're an unlucky boy...

00:23:15.170 --> 00:23:20.510
But, any way, I'm with you.

00:23:20.510 --> 00:23:25.670
So, more and more, keep on doing what you do!

00:23:31.440 --> 00:23:34.640
Attacked by Tarant's forces, we've fled into the temple.

00:23:34.640 --> 00:23:37.170
The elder says that when a crisis befalls the village,

00:23:37.170 --> 00:23:40.340
the statue there will come back to life along with a great fire.

00:23:40.340 --> 00:23:41.680
But it isn't moving at all.

00:23:41.680 --> 00:23:43.750
Next time on Tenchi Muyo GXP!

00:23:43.750 --> 00:23:44.870
Parallel...!?
